# RP2040 boot/connect smoke test. Klipper RP2040 firmware does not
# share generic/armcm_timer.c with the rest of the renode-backed
# Cortex-M ports - it drives the chip's own 64-bit 1MHz timer
# (src/rp2040/timer.c against TIMER_BASE 0x40054000). This test
# exercises that path end-to-end: the C# RP2040_Timer model
# (test/emulator/repl/rp2040_timer.cs, Roslyn-compiled into the
# runtime via `i @file.cs` before LoadPlatformDescription) plus the
# four bit-set synthesis stubs for CLOCKS/RESETS/XOSC/PLL that
# satisfy clock_setup's busy-wait loops. The RPi RP2040 has zero
# upstream Renode coverage (no platform, no peripheral models), so
# this is the only path. printers.test reaches rp2040 via
# generic-bigtreetech-skr-pico-v1.0 at config-parse depth; this is
# the firmware-boot regression target for the C# timer + clock
# stub injection path.
DICTIONARY rp2040.dict
CONFIG rp2040_smoke.cfg
EMULATOR rp2040_smoke.fixture.json

# A few harmless gcode lines so klippy gets past klippy:ready.
M114
M105
M105
M105

# klippy connected and stayed connected long enough to do the
# clocksync handshake against the RP2040_Timer-driven firmware clock.
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "Loaded MCU 'mcu'"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Internal error"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Klippy is shutdown"
